<h3 id="component-selection">Component selection</h3>
<p>Keep Easy Read pages simple. Use a small, consistent set of components so people can focus on the information instead of learning new patterns as they read.</p>
<p>Start with these components:</p>
<table aria-label="Recommended Easy Read components">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th scope="col">Component</th>
      <th scope="col">Use for</th>
      <th scope="col">Link</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">Easy Read content block</th>
      <td>Main information and step-by-step instructions.</td>
      <td><a href="#easy-read-content-block">Easy Read content block section</a></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">Horizontal cards</th>
      <td>Landing and category links to topics or detail pages.</td>
      <td><a href="/components/card/index.html">Card component</a></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">In-page navigation</th>
      <td>Quick movement between sections on longer pages.</td>
      <td><a href="/components/in-page-nav/index.html">In-page nav component</a></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">Utility list</th>
      <td>Downloads and supporting resources.</td>
      <td><a href="/components/utility-list/index.html">Utility list component</a></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">Callout</th>
      <td>Final About Easy Read message and essential supporting context.</td>
      <td><a href="/components/callout/index.html">Callout component</a></td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>Avoid introducing extra components unless user testing shows they improve comprehension. Too many component types on one page can increase cognitive load and make key actions harder to find.</p>

<h4 id="easy-read-content-block">Easy Read content block</h4>
<p>
  The Easy Read content block presents one main idea or action at a time,
  supported by a relevant image. Using this component can help create Easy Read
  content, but does not make a page Easy Read on its own.
</p>
<p>Each content block:</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    Places the image on the left and text on the right, following an established
    Easy Read convention and creating a predictable reading pattern.
  </li>
  <li>
    Uses a white background to keep the content clear and reduce visual
    distraction.
  </li>
  <li>
    Is separated from the next content block by a divider.
  </li>
</ul>

{{#>_docs-example separated=true}}
