<h3 id="search-results-guidance">Search results for Easy Read content</h3>
<p>When Easy Read articles appear in search results, make the format obvious at a glance and keep category information separate.</p>
<ul>
  <li>Use the <strong>label</strong> to identify the format as <strong>Easy Read</strong>.</li>
  <li>Use <strong>tags</strong> for topic categories, such as health, housing or transport.</li>
  <li>Do not use category tags as a substitute for the Easy Read format label.</li>
  <li>Apply this pattern consistently across search, related links and index pages that list mixed content types.</li>
</ul>
<p>Use the <a href="/components/list-item/index.html">list item component</a> pattern to present labels and tags consistently in result lists.</p>


<h2 id="typography-and-styles">3. Typography and styles</h2>
<p>The Easy Read type scale is scoped to <code>nsw-easy-read-content</code>. It increases the standard body and heading sizes by 1.25, rounded to the design system's 4px sub-grid. Landing page card titles use the H4 size so they remain distinct from body text. It does not change standard page typography. Values use <code>rem</code> so browser zoom and text resizing continue to work; the pixel values below are equivalents based on the design system's 16px reference size, not a fixed root font size.</p>
